From: HMU05 thermal work <dev@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8916-generic-hmu05: add Wi-Fi and PMIC thermal mitigation

Bind the wcn36xx firmware thermal-mitigation interface as a cooling device on
the CPU cluster sensor (Wi-Fi) and give pm8916-thermal a cooling device (CPU).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-generic-hmu05.dts | 64 ++++++++++
 1 file changed

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-generic-hmu05.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8916-generic-hmu05.dts
@@ -218,3 +218,67 @@
         line-name = "ftest";
     };
 };
+
+/*
+ * Thermal mitigation for Wi-Fi and PMIC.
+ *
+ * Wi-Fi
+ * -----
+ * The WCN36XX firmware supports WCN36XX_HAL_SET_THERMAL_MITIGATION_REQ: a
+ * mitigation level 0..4 where 0 is normal operation and 1..4 progressively
+ * disable TX AMPDU aggregation and reduce transmit power.  The wcn36xx driver
+ * exposes it as the "wcn36xx" cooling device.
+ *
+ * There is no dedicated WCNSS temperature sensor, so - exactly like Android's
+ * thermal-engine, which applies its "wlan" action once cpu0-1 reaches 60 C -
+ * trigger the mitigation from the CPU cluster sensor (tsens5 / cpu0-1).
+ * OpenWrt idles a few degrees warmer than Android, so the trip is placed at
+ * 65 C (clear of idle, well below the 75 C CPU-throttle trip).
+ *
+ * PMIC
+ * ----
+ * pm8916-thermal has a temperature sensor but no cooling device bound, so
+ * nothing acts on it.  Bind the CPU cooling device: the CPU's SMPS2 rail is the
+ * dominant load on the PMIC, so throttling the CPU also cools the PMIC.
+ */
+
+&wcnss_wifi {
+    #cooling-cells = <2>;
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu0-1-thermal} {
+    trips {
+        wifi_alert: wifi-trip {
+            temperature = <65000>;
+            hysteresis = <3000>;
+            type = "passive";
+        };
+    };
+
+    cooling-maps {
+        wifi_map {
+            trip = <&wifi_alert>;
+            cooling-device = <&wcnss_wifi THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+        };
+    };
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/pm8916-thermal} {
+    trips {
+        pmic_alert: pmic-trip {
+            temperature = <90000>;
+            hysteresis = <5000>;
+            type = "passive";
+        };
+    };
+
+    cooling-maps {
+        pmic_map {
+            trip = <&pmic_alert>;
+            cooling-device = <&CPU0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+                     <&CPU1 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+                     <&CPU2 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+                     <&CPU3 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+        };
+    };
+};
